        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.national-park.com/exploring-the-hidden-charm-of-elkhart-illinois/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Elkhart Historical Society preserves the town’s past with guided tours and living‑history events, keeping stories alive for visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.elkharthistoricalsociety.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1850s the Chicago & Alton Railroad turned Elkhart into a major shipping point, thanks to its large stock‑raising farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elkhart%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A new library building opened in 1904, donated by the Gillett family, and still serves the community today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elkhart%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Elkhart Cemetery holds the graves of many early pioneers and local figures, offering a quiet glimpse into the village’s origins.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
